<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Murong Huang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">297–348</span> · Also known as Emperor Wenming of Former Yan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murong-xianbei">Murong</a> Huang was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a> leader who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/former-yan">Former Yan</a>, declaring himself King of Yan in 337. Building on his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murong-hui">Murong Hui</a>'s settlement of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaoning">Liaoning</a>, he moved his capital to Longcheng (modern Chaoyang) in 342, sacked the Goguryeo capital the same year and destroyed the rival Yuwen Xianbei in 344, making the Murong the strongest power of the north-east.</p></div>
